# CODEOWNERS — viavitae-demos
#
# Each line is a path pattern followed by one or more owners. Later patterns take
# precedence over earlier ones, so the most specific rule wins. Owners are requested
# for review automatically when a matching path changes in a pull request.
#
# Syntax reference: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULE R2 — CODEOWNERS IMMUTABILITY
#
# 1. This file is NEVER empty. An empty CODEOWNERS silently removes every
#    required reviewer, so a pull request that empties it fails review by
#    definition. The `*` rule below must always resolve to at least
#    @JourneyOfLife and @IterVitae.
# 2. Overrides are allowed. Narrower path rules may add or replace owners for
#    their subtree — that is the intended mechanism for giving security,
#    compliance, legal and the DPO authority over their own paths.
# 3. Removal requires compliance team approval. Deleting an owner, widening `*`,
#    or changing the rules for /LICENSE, /SECURITY.md, /QODER.md,
#    /.github/CODEOWNERS, /docs/DPIA-template.md or /.github/workflows/
#    requires an approving review from the compliance reviewer in addition to
#    the standard review. Record the reason as an ADR.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Default owner for everything -------------------------------------------
